  "status": "public-development-corpus-real-fixes",
  "description": "Real public Playwright/Cypress failures whose merged upstream fix is the ground truth. F-code labels are filled from two blind model mappings of the hidden truth; diagnosis labels come from the maintainers' own product/test attribution.",
  "construction_rule": "Each artifact contains only observations: the test identifier, the failure text as reported in the issue, PR, CI log or diff comments (quoted or minimally normalised into a Playwright/Cypress error shape), the pre-fix test code taken from the removed lines and unchanged context of the merged diff, the attempt or frequency pattern the maintainers reported, and environment, DOM, or network facts that a report would show. Sentences that state the cause or the fix were removed and are held in `truth`. Where a report-style detail (a timing in ms, a DOM state at the moment of failure) is not verbatim from the source, it restates a fact the maintainers reported; the source URLs allow an audit of every case.",
